PARITY NOTES (native reproduces the web source's data, composition, states and i18n)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web SessionDetailPanel is a pure, prop-driven presentational component (prop: session: ChargingSession;
  hooks: useTranslation + useFormatting.formatCurrency). It owns NO data source: ChargingCurvePage mounts it
  ONLY once a session is selected from a resolved list, so the page owns the loading / empty / error / stale /
  offline lifecycle. The panel renders a GlassPanel headed "Session Details" with label/value rows:
    Date, Charger Type, SOC Range, Energy Added, Peak Power, [Avg Power], Duration, [Cost], [Location]
  ([] = web conditional: Avg Power iff avg_power_w != null; Cost iff cost_decimal != null; Location iff
  start_place is truthy).

  Native reproduction (SessionDetailPanel.Model.cs = WinUI-free projection; SessionDetailPanel.cs = view):
    - States: model-driven Loading / Empty / Ready, the established presentational-surface precedent
      (ChargingBreakdownSlide): the parent owns the fetch lifecycle, so there is deliberately no fetch-driven
      error / stale / offline branch. The header always renders (never a blank region) — Loading = skeleton
      rows (live region), Empty = "select a session" surface, Ready = the rows via the shared TsKVList.
      Every state carries a Narrator name and is asserted headlessly.
    - Composition / formatting (display boundary; SI stays on the model): Energy Wh/1000 -> "{n} kWh",
      Peak/Avg W/1000 -> "{n} kW", Duration whole-minutes -> "{n} min", all at the web default precision 2
      with en-US grouping via NumberFormatting; Cost via ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency(symbol, 2); Date via
      the shared DateTimeFormatting full variant (em-dash fallback); SOC range "${start}% -> ${end ?? '?'}%"
      via raw number-to-string (matches the JS template literal). The durationMinutes and getChargerLabel
      helpers are ported verbatim (incl. the >20 kW DC-fast threshold and the Tesla/"tesla" Supercharger rule).
    - i18n: 9 of the 10 row labels resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade using the web's exact
      charging.curve.* keys (all present in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw). The Cost row uses the web's
      literal key charging.curve.cost_decimal with the "Cost" fallback: that key is ABSENT from the web i18n
      catalog (web/src/i18n/en.json has charging.curve.cost, not cost_decimal — the field name leaked into the
      key), so the web itself falls back to "Cost". Reproduced byte-for-byte with the same key + fallback (no
      catalog edit: the generated resw mirrors the same JSON that lacks it). The charger-type display values
      (Supercharger / DC Fast / Home / AC) are raw string literals in the web helper; the native port routes
      them through the facade with those exact English fallbacks (charging.curve.charger.*) so the rendered
      value is identical while satisfying "no English literals in native code".
    - Accessibility: the surface AutomationProperties.Name summarises the active state ("Session Details.
      <rows>"); each row carries a "{label} {value}" name; the loading column is announced as a live region.
    - Telemetry: view.opened (slug=SessionDetailPanel) emits on Loaded per the P1/S11 diagnostics contract;
      the diagnostics line is PII-safe (carries only the slug — never a date, place, energy, power or cost).

